Provider-specific image API guidance for Gemini/Nano Banana:
- Reference images are sent as inline image parts. Treat them as guidance, not mandatory content.
  The text brief has priority over copied reference elements.
- Be explicit about what should and should not be reused from references: style, palette, character
  geometry, and source image structure may be reused; unrelated sample labels, logos, and sheet
  artifacts should not.
- Keep geometry and typography simple. If exact generated text may be unreliable, use visual props,
  icons, arrows, and one or two short labels instead of dense wording.
- Be conservative with instrument faces and numeric labels. Gemini may render plausible-looking but
  wrong values; prefer generic gauge markings or explicitly sourced values only.
- Gemini response-format sizing is not forced by default; compose for the requested Anki card role
  and keep the focal content centered with safe margins.
